  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Life saving WASH Assistance to Mitigate against the Impact of Flood on vulnerable Households in Bentiu, Rubkona and Malakal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the onset of 2023 rainy season, the risk of floods i.e. damage and water-borne disease outbreaks in the severely flooded internally displaced persons (IDP) camps and sites in Bentiu and Rubkona, and the highly vulnerable to flood risks Malakal Protection of Civilians (PoC) site is very high. To mitigate against the impact of the floods, this project focuses on preparedness activities geared towards increasing the robustness of existing safe water and sanitation infrastructure in Bentiu, Rubkona IDP camp and Malakal PoC. The main project activities revolve around flood preparedness and flood-resilient infrastructure upgrades and is divided into five components: (1) Upgrade of water supply infrastructure for the rainy season; (2) Upgrade of sanitation infrastructure (latrines and bathing shelters, and collection, disposal, and treatment of faecal matter); (3) Maintenance of faecal sludge management infrastructure and services (desludging and waste stabilization ponds); (4) upgrade of solid waste management infrastructure and services (desludging and waste stabilization ponds); and (5) Prepositioning of water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) non-food items (NFIs) and Information, Education and Communication (IEC) materials for hygiene promotion.</narrative>
  </description>
